==Irish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ga|madradh}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ga|sga|madrad}}, {{m|sga|matrad}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=ga|[ˈmˠad̪ˠɾˠə]}}
* {{audio|ga-madra.ogg|play audio:|lang=ga}}

===Noun===
{{ga-noun|m|-|madraí}}

# [[dog]]
#: {{m|ga||Is teann gach '''madra''' ag a dhoras féin.|lit=Every dog is bold in his own door.|A cock is bold on his own dunghill.}} —Proverb
#: {{m|ga||An té a bhuailfeadh mo '''mhadra''' bhuailfeadh sé mé féin.|lit=Whoever beats my dog beats me.|Love me love my dog.}} —Proverb
#: {{m|ga||Tá an '''madra''' marbh!|lit=The dog is dead!|The fat is in the fire!}}

